From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:00:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/runtime: refuse an imported pipeline binary whose data
 cannot be allocated

vk_create_pipeline_binary allocates the binary and the data it imports in one
object, sizeof(*binary) + data_size, and then copies data_size bytes into it.
The size is the application's, and a size within sizeof(*binary) of SIZE_MAX
wraps the sum to a small allocation that the copy then overruns. Refuse a
size the sum cannot hold with the result an allocation that cannot be
satisfied gives, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, which is what the same function
returns when the allocation fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
index 44474f4e89c3fe39d767d01f40c0161914a565c7..8037fc4136149faab722f44727fc6d5dcc95175c 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -4132,6 +4132,13 @@ vk_create_pipeline_binary(struct vk_device *device,
                        key_size, sizeof(blake3_hash));
    }
 
+   /* The data follows the binary in one allocation, and its size is the
+    * application's: a size near SIZE_MAX wraps the sum below to a small
+    * allocation that the copy then overruns.  A size the allocation cannot
+    * hold is one it cannot satisfy. */
+   if (data_size > SIZE_MAX - sizeof(struct vk_pipeline_binary))
+      return vk_error(device, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY);
+
    struct vk_pipeline_binary *binary =
       vk_object_alloc(device, alloc, sizeof(*binary) + data_size,
                       VK_OBJECT_TYPE_PIPELINE_BINARY_KHR);
